  "rationale": "I'm picking Output B (97) as the winner, with C (94) close behind and A (83) third. B covers every point on the scorecard most completely. On velocity, it gives units, timestamp sampling, velocity handoff into the settle, and a projection formula with a gate on snap choice. It also requires interruption from the current on-screen value, keeps feedback transforms on their own layer, and gives a Reduced Motion path that covers both CSS and JS. Throughout, it marks its numeric values as proposed rather than measured. C is close and very actionable, but it gives slightly less detail on velocity units and transform ownership. A is honest and well ordered but shallower on projection and interruption.",
